      "slug": "crossed-dc",
      "term": "Crossed dc",
      "definition": "Skip 1 stitch, dc into the next stitch, then dc back into the skipped stitch. The two stitches cross to form an X. Both stitches together use the space of 2 stitches."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-chain",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "One chain at the start of each crossed dc row. Does not count as a stitch."
    },
